//? Title: Audio Features: From Samples to Log-Mel Bands
//? Subtitle: Windowing controls leakage; zero-padding changes the grid, not the information
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A sampled waveform is too long and phase-sensitive to use directly as a compact audio feature.
We turn local windows into frequency powers and then into log-mel bands. Tiny exact frames
expose the FFT convention; a generated 1 kHz tone tests window gain, framing and the silence
floor. WAV round trips quantify the separate PCM storage error.
)
\toc

> The method

For a frame of length \(L\), hop \(H\) and FFT length \(N\ge L\), the periodic Hann window is
\(w_n=(1-\cos(2\pi n/L))/2\). The unnormalised transform and power are

$$
X_{t,k}=\sum_{n=0}^{L-1}x_{tH+n}w_n e^{-2\pi i kn/N},\qquad P_{t,k}=|X_{t,k}|^2.
$$
\alttext(Each frame is windowed, transformed without forward normalisation, and squared in magnitude.)

Without padding or centring, a signal of length S has max(0,1+floor((S-L)/H)) frames.
A real transform keeps bins 0 through floor(N/2). For even N, Parseval requires doubling
interior one-sided powers but keeping DC and Nyquist once; divide their sum by N.
The mel coordinate is \(1127\log(1+f/700)\). Unit-height triangles are equally spaced
in mel, their weighted powers are summed, and a natural-log floor prevents log(0).
These are powers, not amplitudes or decibels; no sample-rate conversion occurs.
FFT cost is O(frames N log N); multiplying a dense B-band filter bank costs O(frames N B).

The concept diagram has a retained TikZ source in `diagrams/audio_features_concept.tikz`.
Regeneration requires LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, and dvisvgm.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/audio_features_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/audio_features_concept.tikz > build/audio_features_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/audio_features_concept.svg build/audio_features_concept.dvi > build/audio_features_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered build/audio_features_concept.svg from local TikZ source.\n'
```
